  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Guidance differs",
      "items": [
        "Generator, sampler, controller, metrics and seeds are identical on both sides",
        "TT uses reward gradients at every step; RL uses learned residuals in the final 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Why a critic is needed",
      "items": [
        "Each denoising step adjusts 6,694 numbers — over 66,000 across the guided window",
        "The feedback is a single score, so per-dimension credit is unavailable",
        "A fitted critic supplies that credit, and works when the reward is not differentiable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "This is the Stage 1 setup",
      "items": [
        "Task = tracking human demonstrations, the paper's own protocol",
